WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.990
Automaticity is practiced execution with reduced conscious effort.

00:00:02.990 --> 00:00:07.325
It allows routine components of a task to run smoothly so the

00:00:07.325 --> 00:00:09.493
performer can reserve attention for judgment,

00:00:09.493 --> 00:00:10.577
monitoring, and adaptation.

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:12.744
A skilled operator, engineer, analyst, writer,

00:00:12.744 --> 00:00:17.080
or communicator may perform common steps fluently because those steps have been

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:18.886
practiced many times with feedback.

00:00:18.886 --> 00:00:21.415
Automaticity is powerful because attention is limited.

00:00:21.415 --> 00:00:25.750
Working memory can only hold and process a small amount at once.

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:28.279
If every basic step consumes full attention,

00:00:28.279 --> 00:00:31.169
there is little capacity left for higher-level decisions.

00:00:31.169 --> 00:00:34.782
When routine components become efficient, the performer can notice exceptions,

00:00:34.782 --> 00:00:38.033
coordinate with others, and think about the larger situation.

00:00:38.033 --> 00:00:39.478
The risk is autopilot.

00:00:39.478 --> 00:00:43.091
Fluent behavior can continue even when the situation has changed.

00:00:43.091 --> 00:00:46.703
In high-risk work, experts still need checklists, procedures, deliberate pauses,

00:00:46.703 --> 00:00:51.761
and peer review because memory and attention can fail under pressure, fatigue, or interruption.

00:00:51.761 --> 00:00:53.929
These supports do not replace expertise.

00:00:53.929 --> 00:00:56.458
They protect expertise from predictable human limits.

00:00:56.458 --> 00:00:59.348
Attention control includes focus routines and interruption management.

00:00:59.348 --> 00:01:03.683
Before important work, a performer may clarify the goal, remove avoidable distractions,

00:01:03.683 --> 00:01:07.657
set up required tools, and define when to pause or escalate.

00:01:07.657 --> 00:01:10.547
During the work, they may use checkbacks, notes,

00:01:10.547 --> 00:01:13.437
or short reviews to keep track of assumptions.

00:01:13.437 --> 00:01:17.772
The point is to make attention a managed resource rather than hoping

00:01:17.772 --> 00:01:19.940
it will remain stable by itself.
